<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
  <!-- Shared pattern-call surface for all daemon and Micronaut contracts. -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>PatternKernel</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>recognize</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>bind</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>compose</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>dispatch</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>criticize</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>induce</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:pattern-kernel-calls:v1">SharedPatternKernel</csymbol>
        <list><ci>MicronautPatterns</ci><ci>DaemonPatterns</ci><ci>SraiOperators</ci>
          <ci>aiml-functions</ci><ci>map-filter-fold</ci><ci>CheeseCritic</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
All daemon and Micronaut contracts share this typed pattern-call surface.
Each consumer invokes only the operations appropriate to its role, phase,
scope, and registered capabilities. Shared use does not grant execution rights.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>CallPattern</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>consumer</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>request</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>typedBindings</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>evidenceRefs</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>provenance</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:pattern-kernel-calls:v1">PatternCall</csymbol>
        <ci>consumer</ci><ci>request</ci>
        <list><ci>typedBindings</ci><ci>evidenceRefs</ci><ci>provenance</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Pattern matching and AIML/SRAI redirects resolve typed candidates and bindings.
They do not assert truth, dispatch an unregistered handler, or transfer another
daemon's authority. Dispatch uses local registration and XCFE admission.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Compose</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Fold</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>oplus</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>seed</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Filter</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>Map</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:pattern-kernel-calls:v1">Compose</csymbol>
        <ci>map-filter-fold.mml</ci><ci>typedInputs</ci><ci>declaredOrder</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Map, Filter, and collection Fold are reusable functional transforms described
in map-filter-fold.mml. The consumer declares types, predicates, effects, and
order. Collection Fold is not the K'UHUL six-phase fold lifecycle.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>InducePattern</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>gap</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>sourcePatterns</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>evidence</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>PatternProposal</mi>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>criticReview</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>admission</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:pattern-kernel-calls:v1">FactoryPatternInduction</csymbol>
        <ci>gap</ci><ci>sourcePatterns</ci><ci>evidence</ci><ci>PatternProposal</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
FACTORY-µ may reuse, compose, generalize, specialize, or mutate registered
patterns to address an evidenced capability or coverage gap. Equivalent
patterns are reused instead of duplicated. A material, evidence-backed change
to slots, constraints, or bindings can produce a versioned child proposal with
structural delta, lineage, and provenance. CheeseCritic and applicable
validators review it; registration or activation requires the owner's
authorized admission path. Induction never writes directly to the shared
pattern registry or promotes generated claims to facts.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>DeriveInContext</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>context</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>P_candidate</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>delta</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>lineage</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:pattern-kernel-calls:v1">ContextConditionedPatternDerivation</csymbol>
        <ci>P</ci><ci>context</ci>
        <list><ci>P_candidate</ci><ci>delta</ci><ci>lineage</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
A new context can instantiate or adapt a known pattern. The factory first
canonicalizes and compares candidates: an equivalent pattern is reused, while
a materially different, evidence-backed context produces a derived candidate.
It records changed slots, constraints, bindings, and evidence as a structural
delta. A child retains its parent lineage and never overwrites the parent.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>ValidatePattern</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>P_candidate</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>delta</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>policy</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>valid</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>revise</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>reject</mi><mo>}</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:pattern-kernel-calls:v1">PatternDeltaValidation</csymbol>
        <ci>P_candidate</ci><ci>delta</ci><ci>policy</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Validation checks grammar and types, binding scope, provenance, conflicts,
counterexamples, phase/effect constraints, and the declared novelty or
specialization policy. Similarity to a prior pattern is evidence of lineage,
not proof of correctness. A valid result is a validated proposal; registry
creation or activation still follows explicit owner admission and versioning.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Shared call invariants:
1. Pattern sources are versioned and provenance-bearing.
2. Consumers call registered pattern functions through typed inputs and outputs.
3. Critic results are evidence, not truth or execution permission.
4. Context-derived patterns retain parent lineage and explicit structural deltas.
5. Validation is distinct from registry admission; a validated proposal is not activated automatically.
6. Local XCFE policy and host authorization apply to every state-changing operation.
  </annotation>
</math>
